 ],
 "notes": [
  "sha256 pins: the code objects measured on ctheliosr-1b112-a08-1 (hk/lab/review_tmp/**/*.meta.json of the a08-1 backup) or pinned in Primus-Turbo cade7db6 (manifest.json); a rung without a pin was never built before.",
  "ref_ms: the a08-1 measurement (b4 s8192 hq32 hkv8, lab.py ruler, L2 flush, median), for orientation only; every rung is re-measured in one session on one GPU.",
  "main line f00 -> f10z (written 2026-10-27, e15-02): the order follows what each step needs -- TDM, then double buffering, operand bursts, a 3-slot ring (enabler), software pipelining, then GQA packing on the pipelined kernel; the first-draft order (GQA right after TDM, f03..f08) is kept as a side chain: without a pipeline nothing hides the softmax and every later step stays flat. Steps are over the parent rung."
 ],
